# Build context is the REPO ROOT (render.yaml: dockerContext: .), widened from
# ./live/guild so the committed checkpoint pin can be COPYied into the image.
# Measured cost of that widening: 3.1M -> 5.8M of files, ~7.8M including .git.
# Modest, but the context should not grow unboundedly as history and side
# directories accumulate, so the provably-unneeded parts are excluded here.
#
# CONSERVATIVE BY DESIGN. Every entry below is something no COPY instruction
# references. Nothing that the runtime or the release needs is excluded — in
# particular docs/ is NOT ignored, because docs/checkpoints/latest.json is the
# canonical floor pin the image must carry.
# tests/test_canonical_floor_packaging.py asserts that every Dockerfile COPY
# source survives these rules, so tightening this file cannot silently break
# the build or quietly drop the pin.

# version control and CI definitions — never read at runtime
.git
.github

# language/tool caches and virtualenvs — rebuilt in the image, never copied
**/node_modules
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache

# local scratch
**/.DS_Store
